  <data name="Efi_Elevation_Detail" xml:space="preserve"><value>An EFI folder on a USB stick (or a copy) is read and changed with your rights. An EFI partition can be mounted only by an administrator: for each reading, plan and change the app starts itself once more with administrator rights (Windows asks), mounts the partition at a free drive letter, does that one thing and unmounts it again. A change is made only when the EFI still gives the plan you saw.</value></data>
