  <data name="Eng_Why_Reconnect" xml:space="preserve"><value>with true, OpenCore's RELEASE build boots without a console and watchdogd panics</value></data>
  <data name="Eng_Why_Csr" xml:space="preserve"><value>SIP lets unsigned kexts load from the Auxiliary Kernel Collection</value></data>
  <data name="Eng_Why_Delete" xml:space="preserve"><value>so that the new value replaces the old one at boot</value></data>
  <data name="Eng_Why_SecureBoot" xml:space="preserve"><value>Apple Secure Boot refuses a system volume with a changed seal: needed for the system-volume copy, Safari on the GPU</value></data>
  <data name="Eng_Why_LogTarget" xml:space="preserve"><value>logging on, to a file: opencore-&lt;date&gt;.txt in the root of the EFI volume OpenCore starts from</value></data>
  <data name="Eng_Why_LogDisplay" xml:space="preserve"><value>errors, warnings and info; this only filters the onscreen log, and info lines exist only in DEBUG builds</value></data>
  <data name="Eng_Why_AppleDebug" xml:space="preserve"><value>the macOS boot loader's log goes into OpenCore's log, macOS 10.15.4 and later</value></data>
  <data name="Eng_Why_ApplePanic" xml:space="preserve"><value>the next boot after a kernel panic saves it as panic-&lt;date&gt;.txt in the root of the EFI volume</value></data>
